From 5371477603fb017668e53caf103cd7f717ef32b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:04:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 41/54] engram file layout: one post-hasher break starts every
 Engram layer's row fetch; the layer breaks only join (recipe T3.20 round 2)

The ahead-of-use fetch moved from the first Engram layer's break to a break
right after the hasher: one D2H of both layers' ids, then each table's
worker advises and gathers while layer 0 (first table) and layers 2-13
(second table) run on the GPU. The layer breaks compute the owned mask on
the device instead of a pageable H2D that drained the stream (the ~0.45 ms
GPU gap of a break whose rows were already there). Stale pending fetches
are drained in submit and counted; hit/miss/dropped counts are logged at
power-of-two lookup counts.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
